{
 "_about": "Every foot pair of a ground a body stands on has a step sound (docs/notes/footsteps.md, \"Silent ground\"; exe patch 153 finds the ground of a step on a walker-only floor). A step plays the pair of the foot's material (actor 10 and actor_sprint 53 what others hear, actor_local 42 and actor_local_sprint 56 the player himself, actor_crouch 54 and actor_local_crouch 57 crouched) and the ground's; 33 of the live pairs (patch 27's material.pairs) had no sound, so those steps were silent. Each now plays what the nearest material's pair of the same foot plays, a stock sound (or crouch-steps-1's crouch copy): foliage_dry the plain default step, as 0.69d plays it (a bush rustle there was 9 to 13 dB louder than 0.69d on Mamayev Kurgan's ground), the gratings rabitz's, car glass glass's, the gas tank metall_thin's, the own sprint on mud and bushes their own walking sounds (no own sprint sample exists), others' walking on trunks the wood steps, others' sprint on cars and bodies car metal's and default's. restrictor and actor stay silent (a limiter's faces, another player). A retune is a pair's `to`.",
